("SRN","single registration number","EUDAMED identifier assigned to a registered economic operator.",36),
("CPT","Current Procedural Terminology","AMA code set used for billing U.S. procedures; Category I codes for established services, Category III for emerging ones.",36),
("OS","operating system","Platform software of a scanner or workstation; OS updates are treated as software changes in FDA's change guidance.",36,[36]),
("OTC","over-the-counter","Use without a prescription; moving a device from prescription to OTC use is an intended-use change.",36),
("BMI","body mass index","Weight divided by height squared (kg/m²); a key covariate of ultrasound image quality in subgroup analyses.",36),
("AIB","Artificial Intelligence Board","EU board under the AI Act; issues guidance jointly with the MDCG on AI medical devices.",36),
("VCTE","vibration-controlled transient elastography","Liver stiffness method that tracks a shear wave launched by a mechanical vibrator (the FibroScan principle), reported in kPa.",30),
("MASH","metabolic dysfunction-associated steatohepatitis","Inflammatory form of metabolic fatty liver disease (formerly NASH); a key target for elastography and attenuation imaging.",30),
("WFUMB","World Federation for Ultrasound in Medicine and Biology","International federation that publishes ultrasound guidelines, e.g. on liver elastography and contrast ultrasound.",30),
("LVOT","left ventricular outflow tract","Region just below the aortic valve; its diameter and Doppler VTI give stroke volume and, with the continuity equation, valve area.",29),
("AVA","aortic valve area","Effective orifice area of the aortic valve, usually computed with the continuity equation from LVOT diameter and two VTIs.",29),
("NASCET","North American Symptomatic Carotid Endarterectomy Trial","Trial whose angiographic method of grading carotid stenosis underlies the Doppler velocity criteria.",29),
("ASE","American Society of Echocardiography","Professional society that publishes echocardiography guidelines and measurement conventions.",29),
("EACVI","European Association of Cardiovascular Imaging","European society that co-publishes echocardiography guidelines with the ASE.",29),
("LI-RADS","Liver Imaging Reporting and Data System","ACR system for categorizing liver observations in patients at risk of hepatocellular carcinoma; a CEUS version defines enhancement-based categories.",28),
("APHE","arterial phase hyperenhancement","Enhancement in the arterial phase greater than the surrounding liver; a major LI-RADS feature.",28),
("HCC","hepatocellular carcinoma","Primary liver cancer; the main target of LI-RADS categorization.",28),
("DCE-US","dynamic contrast-enhanced ultrasound","Quantitative contrast ultrasound: time–intensity curves are fitted to derive perfusion parameters.",28),
("GUM","Guide to the Expression of Uncertainty in Measurement","The JCGM/ISO reference method for combining measurement uncertainties; used for tolerance and test-limit budgets.",17),
("FMEA","failure mode and effects analysis","Structured review of how each part or process step can fail, its effect and its detectability; used in design and process risk management.",17),
("P–E","polarization–electric field (loop)","Hysteresis loop of a ferroelectric's polarization versus applied field; gives the coercive field and remanent polarization.",16),
("ISSCC","International Solid-State Circuits Conference","IEEE conference where integrated ultrasound front-end and probe ASICs are often first reported.",18),
("nIVD","non-IVD","FDA eSTAR version for devices other than in vitro diagnostics.",36),
("MDCG","Medical Device Coordination Group","EU group of national authorities that issues MDR guidance documents (MDCG yyyy-n), e.g. on classification, clinical evaluation and PSURs.",36),
("IIa","EU device class IIa","Medium-risk class under MDR Annex VIII; diagnostic ultrasound is IIa by Rule 10, so a notified body must assess the QMS and technical documentation.",36),
("IIb","EU device class IIb","Higher-risk class under MDR Annex VIII; Rule 10 puts devices for monitoring vital parameters, where variations could mean immediate danger, in IIb.",36),
("NB","notified body","Organization designated by an EU member state to assess conformity of Class IIa and higher devices (QMS audit and technical-documentation review).",36),
("NANDO","New Approach Notified and Designated Organisations","European Commission database listing notified bodies and the MDR scope each is designated for.",36),
("CE","CE marking","Mark showing conformity with EU legislation; for Class IIa and higher devices it requires a notified-body certificate.",36,[36]),
